senses
  entry
    definition "the vertical force exerted by a mass as a result of gravity"
    id oewn-05034009-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "sports equipment used in calisthenic exercises and weightlifting; it is not attached to anything and is raised and lowered by use of the hands and arms"
    id oewn-04578578-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("free weight" "exercising weight")
  entry
    definition "the relative importance granted to something"
    examples ("his opinion carries great weight" "the progression implied an increasing weightiness of the items listed")
    id oewn-05179849-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (weightiness)
  entry
    definition "an artifact that is heavy"
    id oewn-04578374-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "an oppressive feeling of heavy force"
    examples ("bowed down by the weight of responsibility")
    id oewn-07554200-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a system of units used to express the weight of something"
    id oewn-13737860-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("system of weights")
  entry
    definition "a unit used to measure weight"
    examples ("he placed two weights in the scale pan")
    id oewn-13630031-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("weight unit")
  entry
    definition "(statistics) a coefficient assigned to elements of a frequency distribution in order to represent their relative importance"
    id oewn-13610524-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (weighting)
  entry
    definition "weight down with a load"
    id oewn-01489937-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (burden burthen "weight down")
  entry
    definition "present with a bias"
    examples ("He biased his presentation so as to please the share holders")
